<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan allows Bank of East Asia to open branch.</title>
<headline>Taiwan allows Bank of East Asia to open branch.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's finance ministry agreed to let Hong Kong-based Bank of East Asia establish a branch office on the island, a ministry statement said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank opened a representative office in Taipei in April 1993.</p>
<p>It has 74 branches in Hong Kong, six branches and five representative offices in mainland China, and 10 overseas branch offices.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
